.MARINE...
(Today through Saturday)
Issued at 1026 AM PDT Mon Sep 28 2026

High pressure strengthening over the Eastern Pacific will maintain
moderate to strong northerly breezes through Wednesday. Strongest
winds will be outer water north of Point Reyes and the Big Sur
Coast. Rough seas will build in response to these winds and will
subside to moderate by the end of the week due to northerly winds
becoming light to moderate. Tropical activity will produce long
period swell up to 16 seconds Wednesday and Thursday.

